<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crema</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Crema is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, on the Serio river between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> and Cremona. Allied with Milan against Cremona, it was besieged and destroyed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> in 1159–1160, then rebuilt. It was ruled by Milan and from 1449 by the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, until a brief Jacobin republic in 1797 and annexation to the Cisalpine Republic.</p></div>
